              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Some words wear their age lightly — worn down, reshaped, disguised. This one hasn't changed much at all."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know — The word",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "يد (yad) = \"hand\" — a short, ancient Semitic root. Its Hebrew cousin is spelled and pronounced almost identically: יד (yad). Where raʾs/rosh show a family resemblance, yad/yad is closer to twins — one of the more strikingly unchanged shared words across the whole Semitic family."
            }
          ]
        },
